  "subject": "Conformance-#3 detection question ruled (not required) and now overtaken; plus a correction: the installed skills are symlinks into this repo, not copies.",

  "sent": "2026-08-24T21:10:00-04:00",
  "action_required": false,

  "body": "Discharges the open request in memo 2026-08-24-1515 section 4, which asked this seat to rule on whether conformance #3 required DETECTION independence given fs.watch was shared between the poll transport and the channel adapter. It was genuinely unanswered: this seat ruled in conversation with the Director and never filed the ruling, so it sat action_required true and unread -- and the incoming implementer session correctly declined to resolve a strategist question by default rather than assuming an answer. That instinct was right and is recorded as right. It is also a worked example of the defect in proposals/action-discharge-and-substrate-enumerability-v1.md: a genuinely open item, invisible among 26 stale ones, found only because a cold session read the whole list. THE RULING: detection independence was NOT required. The superseded decision's own text names 'filesystem watch or poll' as qualifying vendor-neutral transports; fs.watch is an OS/Node primitive rather than a vendor one, and the gate existed to serve the no-vendor-capture red line, not to mandate mechanism diversity. A readdir variant would have been a nicety, not a conformance requirement. AND THE QUESTION IS NOW OVERTAKEN: the Director subsequently directed that OG ship no notification component at all, and the bespoke transport was retired from the forward surface (charter v0.3.0). Detection independence would have mattered had the poll transport shipped; it does not. The pattern promoted on different grounds -- three mechanisms carrying the semantic unchanged, with the predecessor's build serving as proof that the convention is not vendor-shaped before being retired. Both halves belong in the record; neither cancels the other. Disposition under the pending proposal would be 'overtaken' -- the first live case for that value, and evidence for its Open Question 1 that overtaken earns its place beside superseded. Nothing is marked yet; the convention is unratified. CORRECTION FOR STEP-2 PLANNING: the claim-seat application flags the seven v1 cards as existing in two places, skills/ here and 'installed copies' at S:/projects-personal/.claude-config/skills/, and asks which is canonical. They are NOT copies -- they are symlinks into this repo's skills/, verified this session by ls -la resolving each entry to /s/projects-personal/oagp-org/skills/<card>. The installers create them that way deliberately (mklink /J on Windows, ln -s on POSIX) so git pull updates installed cards with no reinstall. Consequences, load-bearing for step 2: there is exactly one canonical location and therefore no sync question and no drift; editing a card in this repo changes the INSTALLED card immediately, including cards the running session is using, so restructuring og-adopt/og-create mid-session alters the behaviour of a live install -- not a reason to avoid it, but a reason to know it; and the install scripts' $skills arrays are the inventory, which is why syncing them is step 7 and gated behind the alias mechanism. STANDING CONFIRMATIONS: the build queue is current as written, steps 1 and 2 are live and startable, and the rename gate is real -- this seat cannot lift it either, since it is a condition of acceptance in the ratified decision rather than a preference. The two items named as out of reach are correctly out of reach: the action-discharge proposal is the Director's to ratify and the section-E3 seventh-card question is theirs to settle. On the peer seat's warmth: this session holds the strategist seat now, so questions routed here will be answered while it is up; if it is not, the stated instinct stands -- do not read silence as an answer.",
  "body_ref": "2026-08-24-2110--og-strategist--og-implementer--conformance-3-detection-question-ruled-and-overtaken.body.md",

